by GromNaN at 2026-10-17T21:32:10Z

Thanks @mindaugasvcs for raising these two problems in #59042.

The display rotation is now read from the display matrix, so the width, height, pixel and ratio checks use the dimensions as they are displayed. A portrait video encoded as 1920x1080 with a 90 degree rotation is no longer reported as landscape.

Streams that are attached pictures, like a thumbnail or a cover art, are now rejected instead of being validated as a video.

A file whose only video stream is a single frame is still accepted for now, since the existing test fixtures are single frame videos.

