by nicolas-grekas at 2026-10-18T09:10:17Z

PR updated. ffprobe only knows `stream_side_data` since FFmpeg 5.1, and older versions fail on the whole option. On Ubuntu 22.04 (FFmpeg 4.4), every video would have been reported as corrupted. `stream_side_data_list` works with all versions.

Attached pictures are now also ignored when counting streams. Before, a video with a cover art was rejected for having multiple streams, or as a thumbnail when the cover came first.

